      "headline": "Pemex admits Gulf of Mexico oil spill originated from its pipeline; three officials fired amid environmental backlash",
      "summary": "After weeks of denials, the Mexican government confirmed on April 16\u201317 that a February oil spill affecting over 900 km of Veracruz and Tabasco coastline originated from a ruptured Pemex pipeline near the Cantarell complex. Three Pemex officials were dismissed for concealing the information; Sheinbaum ordered a permanent Gulf monitoring observatory. Environmental NGOs, opposition legislators, and Oceana called the personnel actions insufficient and demanded full disclosure of spill volumes, remediation costs, and criminal accountability. Separately, Pemex reported a new unrelated hydrocarbon leak at an abandoned well in Minatitl\u00e1n, Veracruz.",
